==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌtæm.bəˈɹiːn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-tambourine.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|tam|bour|ine|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|tambourin||little drum}}, from {{m|fr|tambour||drum}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{l|en|A [[percussion]] [[musical instrument|instrument]] consisting of a small, usually wooden, hoop closed on one side with a [[drum]] frame and featuring [[jingle|jingling]] metal disks on the tread; it is most often held in the hand and shaken [[rhythmic]]ally; by extension, any [[frame drum]].}}
# A {{l|en|tambourine dove}}.
#* '''2006''', Gayle Soucek, ''Doves'' (page 78)
#*: '''Tambourines''' are shy birds and do not tame easily.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|tambourinist}}

